<p>Columns can be aligned to the left, the center or the right.</p>
<h2>Code</h2>
<p>Inline <code>code</code> and code blocks keep every character as written:</p>
<pre lang="rust"><code>fn main() {
    println!("Hello from Markdown Editor");
}
</code></pre>
<pre lang="sh"><code>shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS
</code></pre>
<pre><code>An indented block is code as well.
</code></pre>
<h2>Links</h2>
<p>A click on a link in the preview never opens it: the app copies the
address and shows the real host in a short notice. Try it with
<a href="https://github.com/droczy/markdown-editor" rel="noopener noreferrer">the project on GitHub</a>.</p>
<p>Web addresses such as <a href="https://example.com" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://example.com</a> and <a href="http://www.example.org" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.example.org</a> become links
by themselves. A click on an email link copies only the address:
<a href="mailto:someone@example.com?subject=Hello" rel="noopener noreferrer">write to someone</a>.</p>
<h2>Things to try in the app</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Zoom</strong> editor and preview together with <em>View &gt; Zoom In</em> (⌘+),
<em>Zoom Out</em> (⌘−) and <em>Actual Size</em> (⌘0). The zoom level is kept.</li>
<li><strong>Light and dark:</strong> switch the appearance in <em>System Settings</em>, and the
preview follows.</li>
<li><strong>Autosave:</strong> every change is saved on its own; earlier versions are
under <em>File &gt; Revert To</em>.</li>
<li><strong>Privacy:</strong> <em>Help &gt; Privacy and Permissions</em> explains what the app may
do, and what it never does. It works offline and sends nothing anywhere.</li>
</ul>
<p>The <a href="https://github.com/droczy/markdown-editor/blob/main/FEATURES.md" rel="noopener noreferrer">feature list</a>
describes everything in detail, including what is planned.</p>
